message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Structural and Practical Identifiability of a Shared Metabolic Cancer ODE under Multi-Channel Noisy Observation Maps"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can a shared metabolic ODE recover unique (or practically unique) parameters
  from multi-channel metabolomics-style outputs, or does identifiability
  collapse under realistic noisy maps? For a four-state glucose, pyruvate,
  lactate and glutamine-pool model, a steady lactate/glucose ratio has Fisher
  rank 1 of 5. A four-channel snapshot with a lineage loading has profiled
  rank 4 of 5: a common rescaling of the rates is absorbed by the loading, so
  coordinate profiles stay flat. A scale gauge and a time-course upper bound
  are reported separately. Draws are a synthetic surrogate, not a CCLE file.
  Not a medical device.
keywords:
